{"id":"5efb24d5420b1f28737e4e8d1b62b354ddc18069","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"5efb24d5420b1f28737e4e8d1b62b354ddc18069","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/features/sleep_mode.md","lines":["@@ -156,6 +156,17 @@ llm.release_kv_cache_memory()"," llm.wake_up(tags=[\"kv_cache\"])  # Reallocate KV cache and resume scheduling."," ```"," ","+#### Keep the KV connector cache","+","+Discarding the KV cache, by a sleep at level 1 or 2 or by `release_kv_cache_memory()`, also resets a configured KV connector's cache, such as blocks offloaded to CPU or kept in an external store. Pass `reset_connector=False` to keep it, so that requests after the wake-up load those blocks instead of recomputing them:","+","+```python","+llm.sleep(level=1, reset_connector=False)","+llm.wake_up()","+```","+","+Block hashes do not cover the weights. If the weights may change before the wake-up, keep the default, or give requests a `cache_salt` per weight version so that blocks computed with older weights are never matched.","+"," #### Offloading CUDA graph memory"," "," By default, CUDA graph memory stays on the GPU while asleep. With","@@ -252,8 +263,8 @@ curl -X POST 'http://localhost:8000/wake_up?tags=kv_cache'"," "," #### HTTP endpoints"," ","-- `POST /sleep?level=1` — Put the model to sleep (`level=1`).","-- `POST /release_kv_cache_memory` — Discard KV cache memory after a completed pause, while all executor memory is resident.","+- `POST /sleep?level=1` — Put the model to sleep (`level=1`). `reset_connector=false` keeps the KV connector's cache.","+- `POST /release_kv_cache_memory` — Discard KV cache memory after a completed pause, while all executor memory is resident. `reset_connector=false` keeps the KV connector's cache."," - `POST /wake_up` — Wake up the model. Supports optional `tags` query parameters for partial wake-up (e.g., `?tags=weights`)."," - `POST /collective_rpc` — Perform a collective remote procedure call (RPC)."," - `GET /is_sleeping` — Check if the model is sleeping."],"additions":13,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/training/async_rl.md","lines":["@@ -37,6 +37,12 @@ such as `sleep`, keep queueing new requests."," "," The `clear_cache` parameter controls whether to clear the KV cache and prefix cache after pausing."," ","+`clear_cache=True` also resets a configured KV connector's cache. To clear only the local caches,","+pause with `clear_cache=False`, then call","+`reset_prefix_cache(reset_running_requests=True, reset_connector=False)`. Block hashes do not cover","+the weights, so keep the connector's cache only if the weights do not change, or give requests a","+`cache_salt` per weight version.","+"," ### resume_generation"," "," ```python"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -5838,7 +5838,7 @@ dependencies = ["," "," [[package]]"," name = \"vllm-proto\"","-version = \"0.6.0\"","+version = \"0.7.0\""," dependencies = [","  \"prost\",","  \"prost-types\","],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/proto/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@"," [package]"," name = \"vllm-proto\"","-version = \"0.6.0\"","+version = \"0.7.0\""," edition.workspace = true"," license.workspace = true"," description = \"Protobuf messages and gRPC bindings for the vLLM Rust frontend\""],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/proto/README.md","lines":["@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ the schemas on pull requests, including on forks."," "," ```toml"," [dependencies]","-vllm-proto = \"0.6\"","+vllm-proto = \"0.7\""," ```"," "," For example, import `vllm_proto::inference_client::InferenceClient` or"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/proto/control.proto","lines":["@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@ message IsPausedResponse { bool paused = 1; }"," message SleepRequest {","   optional uint32 level = 1;","   PauseMode mode = 2;","+  optional bool reset_connector = 3;"," }"," message SleepResponse {}"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":